# Exclude large/irrelevant directories from the Docker build context.
# Only guest/modules/, guest/*.c, guest/*.h, and docker/ are needed.
#
# guest/out/ matters more than it looks: a plain host `make` uses the musl
# cross-compiler, and its .o files landing in the build context make the
# container's `make shim` a no-op ("Nothing to be done"). The musl shim then
# ships in place of the glibc one and every process that preloads it dies with
# "libc.so: cannot open shared object file" - EP122 included. Keep the container
# building from sources only.
guest/out/
build/
dist/
target/
.git/
app/
tools/
initramfs-patch/
qemu/
crates/
docs/
